<title>USA: U.S. advertising revs seen up 6.2 percent in 1997.</title>
<headline>U.S. advertising revs seen up 6.2 percent in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total U.S. advertising revenue is expected to increase 6.2 percent to $186 billion in 1997, McCann-Erickson Worldwide advertising agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Robert Coen, senior vice-president and director of forescasting at McCann, a unit of Interpublic Group of Cos Inc, said he expects national advertising to jump six percent this year to about $109.2 billion, while local advertising will rise 6.4 percent to about $76.8 billion.</p>
</text>
